  "metadata": {
    "alignment": "standard",
    "description": "eugr's (Eugene Rakhmatulin) spark-vllm-docker diffusion-gemma-bf16 recipe for Google's DiffusionGemma-26B-A4B-it (bf16; checkpoint revision f7f5b7f5), Apache-2.0, served by vLLM on a single Spark. Runs eugr's published vllm-node image (nightly-20260929, digest pinned; its build-metadata records spark-vllm-docker 42f62e34, vLLM 0.30.1rc1.dev336+gaf5b4857e and FlashInfer 4a638133) with upstream's launch: block-diffusion decoding (canvas length 256), TRITON_ATTN attention, fastsafetensors loading, prefix caching, gemma4 reasoning and tool-call parsers, 262,144-token context and memory utilisation 0.8 (upstream defaults), ten sequences and Triton MoE backend. Upstream's diffusiongemma mod is applied at image build time: it skips its vLLM patches because the pinned image already contains DiffusionGemma support and only installs its no-thinking chat template at /workspace/vllm/fixed_chat_template.jinja, which the recipe passes by absolute path (upstream uses a path relative to its working directory). Thinking is an option: the default is upstream's diffusion-gemma-bf16 (thinking off, fixed chat template); the other choice is eugr's diffusion-gemma-bf16-thinking recipe (enable_thinking true with the checkpoint's own chat template). The upstream recipe is solo-only. No upstream performance claims are recorded. Upstream repository MIT. Physical Spark acceptance is pending.",
    "tags": [
      "bf16",
      "candidate",
      "diffusion",
      "diffusiongemma",
      "eugr",
      "executable",
      "gemma",
      "reasoning",
      "single",
      "spark",
      "tool-use",
      "vllm"
    ],
    "title": "DiffusionGemma 26B-A4B bf16 vLLM single Spark (eugr)"
